---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SourcesFooter from "../../components/SourcesFooter.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy · AfroTech 2026 Planner" active="none" description="What the AfroTech 2026 Planner stores, and how to delete it.">
  <article class="privacy">
    <h1>Privacy: you can use everything without signing in</h1>
    <p>
      The planner is a free, ad-free community site. Without an account, nothing about you leaves your
      device: your plan, your notes (photos included) and your theme live in your browser's storage.
    </p>

    <h2>If you sign in with Google</h2>
    <p>Signing in is optional and only syncs your plan and notes across your devices. We store:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your Google account id, email address, name and profile picture link, as Google provides them.</li>
      <li>The events you've starred or unstarred, with the time of each change.</li>
      <li>
        Your notes: each note's title, text, session and times. Only you can read them; nobody else can see
        them on the site. A deleted note is kept as an empty record so the deletion reaches your other devices.
      </li>
      <li>
        Photos you add to notes, shrunk on your device before they upload. They're stored privately with
        your account and shown only to you; there's no public link to them. Deleting a note, or taking a
        photo out of it, deletes the photo.
      </li>
      <li>A session record so you stay signed in for 30 days. We keep only a scrambled form of the session key.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We don't store Google passwords or tokens, ask for any other Google data, sell or share anything, or use
      ads or tracking cookies. Our only cookie is the session cookie that keeps you signed in. On the Saved tab,
      Google's sign-in button loads Google's own script, which may set a small cookie to remember your
      sign-in choices; <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a> covers it.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
    <p>
      On <a href="/plan/">Saved</a>, tap <strong>Delete my data</strong>. Your account, sessions, saved plan,
      notes and photos are deleted at once. The copies on your device stay until you clear them. Signing out instead
      keeps everything in your account and removes your notes and photos from that device, so they stay private on a
      shared phone or laptop.
    </p>

    <h2>Your location</h2>
    <p>
      "Near me" uses your location only when you tap it, and only inside your browser. It is never sent to us.
    </p>

    <h2>Speaker profiles</h2>
    <p>
      Speaker bios, photos and links come from the official AfroTech schedule. Researched facts appear only
      after review, each with its source. Speakers can ask for changes or removal by opening an issue on
      <a href="https://github.com/laudebugs/afrotech/issues">GitHub</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Who runs this</h2>
    <p>
      The planner is run by <a href="https://github.com/laudebugs">laudebugs</a>. It isn't affiliated with
      AfroTech or Blavity. Questions go to <a href="https://github.com/laudebugs/afrotech/issues">GitHub issues</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
  <SourcesFooter />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
  }
  h2 {
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
  }
  li {
    margin: var(--space-1) 0;
  }
</style>
